"answer": "Project Zenith is a new initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics, led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off scheduled for June 15th. The project initially had a phase one budget of $500,000, which was later increased to $2 million approved by the executive board to cover research, development, and marketing. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% efficiency increase using AI algorithms. The team has expanded with new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing, with onboarding sessions scheduled for September 10th and April 15th, 2023. Training budgets of $15,000 have been approved for coding teams and project managers. Key milestones include the completion of the testing phase, celebrated on October 10th. Upcoming activities include a meeting on August 5th to discuss findings, a budget discussion on August 1st, and a request for stakeholder feedback on the prototype by the end of November. Additionally, a confirmation email is required to be sent to contact@contact.com to secure approvals for the next stages."
